SWEET nav General-row probe (patch 0269, sprint-gpu 2026-11-08, user OK to fix the General tap; input choice only, read-only framebuffer scan, no register, no store to hardware): before the general-open tap the nav session (patch 0243) asks sweet_fb_probe_general() for the General row of the Settings root list in the last presented layer-0 surface (icon column touch x 40..215: first grey run >= 30 rows below a purple Focus/Screen Time row) and taps its centre; implausible / not found = the calibrated 500,1900 + 'SWEET GAP: NAV general-open'. Logs 'SWEET NAV: general probe rep R rc C y Y runs N purple_last P -> tap 500,T'. Reason [obs camera frames nav27 r1, nav31 r1-2]: the list's resting scroll offset after settings-scroll-down varies by ~50-150 touch px, so the fixed 1900 hit the section gap or Screen Time.
